sequenceDiagram
    %% AgentUML: Orchestrator-Worker Pattern
    %% Pattern: Central LLM routes subtasks to specialised workers, then synthesises
    %% Context-Window Risk: HIGH — orchestrator accumulates ALL worker outputs
    %% before replying. With N workers, prompt grows linearly → overflow risk.

    participant U as User
    participant G as Input Guardrail <<guardrail>>
    participant O as Orchestrator <<orchestrator>>
    participant M as Working Memory <<memory_working>>
    participant VS as Vector Store <<memory_semantic>>
    participant W1 as Web Search Worker <<agent>>
    participant W2 as Code Analyst Worker <<agent>>
    participant W3 as SQL Query Worker <<agent>>
    participant LLM as Gemini LLM <<llm>>

    U->>G: 1. Send prompt
    G-->>O: 2. Approve (policy pass) [deterministic guardrail]

    O->>M: 3. Load conversation history
    O->>VS: 4. Retrieve semantic context (RAG)
    VS-->>O: 5. Return top-k documents

    O->>LLM: 6. Decompose task → subtask plan

    %% Parallel fan-out to workers
    par Worker Fan-Out [non-deterministic latency]
        O->>W1: 7a. Web search subtask
        O->>W2: 7b. Code analysis subtask
        O->>W3: 7c. SQL query subtask
    end

    W1-->>O: 8a. Observation (appended to context ⚠️)
    W2-->>O: 8b. Observation (appended to context ⚠️)
    W3-->>O: 8c. Observation (appended to context ⚠️)

    Note over O,M: ⚠ HIGH OVERFLOW RISK: orchestrator context window<br/>grows with each worker response. Monitor token budget.

    O->>M: 9. Append all observations
    O->>LLM: 10. Synthesise final answer from full context
    LLM-->>O: 11. Final synthesis

    O-->>U: 12. Deliver response
